# S0c: the REFERENCE for A1 and H1-H5: the same attach on the CONTROL profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-time-gate (every W1 lever off), with the tests the exactness READ rules compare against:
# warmup, one coding stream, concurrent8_steady (the quad blocks' mix: the quad-blocks smoke rule needs it), concurrent8_code_32k and the exactness reference concurrent8_code_equal.
# READ: admission passed at capacity 262144, every answer completes, c2_smoke_check clean, no stall. RECORD per request the answer hash, the accepted tokens and the verify rounds (concurrent8_code_32k,
# concurrent8_code_equal): A1 and H1-H5 must equal this run on the answer hashes (the audited attach compares concurrent8_code_32k; the audits-off hang shapes compare concurrent8_code_equal). Duration (estimate): 90 min. Stop rule.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/w1 eight-seat 262k stack window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/w1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w1-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/w1 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w1-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-time-gate
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_equal
